<span id="Introduction"></span>
== Úvod ==

[[Image:Workbench_Robot.svg|24px]] [[Robot_Workbench/cs|Pracovní prostředí Robot]] je nástroj pro simulaci standardního [[Robot_6-Axis/cs|šestiosého průmyslového robota]], jako je například [http://kuka.com/ Kuka].

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
You can do the following tasks:
* Set up a simulation environment with a robot and work pieces.
* Create and fill up movement trajectories.
* Decompose features of a CAD part to a trajectory.
* Simulate the robot movement and reaching distance.
* Export the trajectory to a robot program file.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
To get started try the [[Robot_tutorial|Robot tutorial]], and see the programming interface in the [https://github.com/FreeCAD/FreeCAD_sf_master/blob/master/src/Mod/Robot/RobotExample.py RobotExample.py] example file.
</div>

[[Image:Robot_Workbench_example.jpg|500px]]

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
== Tools ==
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
=== Robot toolbar ===
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
* [[Image:Robot_CreateRobot.svg|32px]] [[Robot_CreateRobot|Place Robot]]: Places a robot in the model.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
* [[Image:Robot_CreateTrajectory.svg|32px]] [[Robot_CreateTrajectory|Trajectory]]: Creates an empty trajectory.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
* [[Image:Robot_InsertWaypoint.svg|32px]] [[Robot_InsertWaypoint|Insert in Trajectory]]: Inserts a robot tool position into a trajectory.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
* [[Image:Robot_InsertWaypointPre.svg|32px]] [[Robot_InsertWaypointPre|Insert in Trajectory (vertex)]]: Inserts a preselected position into a trajectory.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
* [[Image:Robot_Edge2Trac.svg|32px]] [[Robot_Edge2Trac|Edge to Trajectory]]: Generates a trajectory from selected edges.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
* [[Image:Robot_TrajectoryDressUp.svg|32px]] [[Robot_TrajectoryDressUp|Dress-Up Trajectory]]: Creates a dress-up object that overrides aspects of a trajectory.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
* [[Image:Robot_TrajectoryCompound.svg|32px]] [[Robot_TrajectoryCompound|Trajectory Compound]]: Groups and connects multiple trajectories into one.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
* [[Image:Robot_SetHomePos.svg|32px]] [[Robot_SetHomePos|Set Home Position]]: Sets the home position of a robot.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
* [[Image:Robot_RestoreHomePos.svg|32px]] [[Robot_RestoreHomePos|Move to Home]]: Moves a robot to its home position.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
* [[Image:Robot_Simulate.svg|32px]] [[Robot_Simulate|Simulate Trajectory]]: Simulates robot movement along a selected trajectory.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
=== Other tools ===
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
* Insert Robot:
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
:* [[Image:Robot_AddToolShape.svg|32px]] [[Robot_AddToolShape|Tool]]: Adds a tool shape to a robot.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
* [[Robot_SetDefaultOrientation|Set Default Orientation]]: Sets the default orientation for subsequent waypoint creation.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
* [[Robot_SetDefaultValues|Set Default Values]]: Sets the default values for speed, acceleration, and continuity for subsequent waypoint creation.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
* Export Trajectory:
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
:* [[Image:Robot_ExportKukaCompact.svg|32px]] [[Robot_ExportKukaCompact|Kuka Compact Subroutine]]: Exports a trajectory as a compact KRL subroutine.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
:* [[Image:Robot_ExportKukaFull.svg|32px]] [[Robot_ExportKukaFull|Kuka Full Subroutine]]: Exports a trajectory as a full KRL subroutine.
</div>

